    "notes": "Exact victim depletion measured from receipts: for every market in the Cream Comptroller's getAllMarkets() at block 13499797, the net movement of that market's own underlying() token across the nine successful campaign transactions, plus native-ETH flows for crETH. Fifty-seven ERC-20 markets and crETH are net negative and every recipient is one of the two attacker contracts. Attacker-supplied flash-loan principal is excluded because it is netted inside the same measurement; the recursive crYUSD leg therefore contributes only 1,424.188372514512394279 yUSD. Fifty-two components use DefiLlama historical prices for the anchor timestamp; six underlyings with no DefiLlama series (yvCurve-stETH, HBTC, vVSP, yvCurve-IronBank, ibBTC, yUSD) use Cream's own unmanipulated getUnderlyingPrice at block 13499797 converted at the same DefiLlama ETH price and are marked method other. The 144.4 million total exceeds the ~130 million commonly reported; the gap is concentrated in thin-market components (CRETH2 at 39.9 million, RUNE, wNXM, PERP) which are marked at contemporaneous quotes and which the attacker could not have liquidated at those quotes, so realised attacker proceeds were lower than this gross victim depletion."
  },
